comments.text:
Owner decision, 2026-10-09: this feature also takes the wiki's layout shell, not only its typography. Reference: a design mockup the owner made with another agent ("Madarch Wiki v2", a static prototype on CodeMirror 6, not kept in the repository); a reference, not a target: values may be improved or changed.

Added to the scope:
- a left navigation: the product's name and its documents grouped by kind (product, requirements, decisions, research), the current page highlighted, any other page one click away;
- the document in the centre as the main element;
- a focus mode that hides the panels;
- on a phone the navigation moves into a menu instead of squeezing the document;
- a place for a right context panel, closed by default and empty until madarch-fe1 (links both ways) and madarch-0uc (open questions) fill it.
Still out: search, the editor, the Markdown and history modes, the chat (madarch-j0a, madarch-cuu).

The owner's feedback on the mockup, kept as conditions:
- a first version with a green accent was rejected ("green will not suit everyone; the fonts are small"); the second, neutral graphite with larger text, was accepted as a direction;
- no brand colour, and no smaller interface, without discussing it with the owner;
- the dark theme follows the system setting.

The mockup's values, a starting point for madarch-iuc.1 to check: body 18 px, line height about 1.58 to 1.6, measure 60 to 75 characters; page title 40 px wide, 32 px on a phone; navigation 14 px, secondary text mostly 12 px.

Found when the mockup was rendered at 1440, 1150 and 390 px in both themes (no horizontal overflow at any width), to fix in this feature:
- the mockup names Inter but does not ship it, so Linux fell back to DejaVu Sans: ship the fonts (Inter and a monospace face under the OFL, Cyrillic included);
- its icons are Unicode symbols, half of them missing on Linux: use SVG icons;
- a 740 px column at 18 px Inter gives about 80 to 85 characters: set the measure in em, about 36 to 38;
- on a phone the mode switch and the file name crowd the toolbar;
- the grey secondary text at 9 to 10 px needs a measured contrast check.

Size: about half a day of agent time instead of one to two hours.

description:
The plugin's setup version (0.26.0, plugin 0.57.1) is newer than the repository's installed checks (rules 0.24.0), so every skill that writes asks for setup first.

## Done when
- the three shipped checks are the 0.26.0 copies, byte for byte, and their selftests pass;
- one committed command connects a fresh clone (hooks, filter, tracker import and path migration, private patterns), is safe to rerun, and fails naming what is missing; the privacy guard refuses a commit when it has no pattern list (absorbs madarch-xh6);
- the integration's claim operation holds a same-stage dependant of an implemented prerequisite atomically, keeping the edge (absorbs madarch-5db);
- the evidence revision leaves out exactly the tracker export, the change records, the current specs and their catalogue, and the integration names those paths;
- a commit is asked for a change only for what it delivers (code, documents, a tracker transition to submitted, implemented or closed); a tracker-only commit that files or comments needs none;
- every proof of the setup skill's section 4 is run and recorded on this task; the installation lands on main.

## Left out
Changing any product code or settings; the profile is kept.

Change registry-integrity, capability server: requirements identities (id part). A canonical serialization (JSON, keys sorted by code point, no insignificant whitespace) and its SHA-256 digest, as one reusable function with tests; the server assigns each source a stable opaque id on first send, keeps it across sends and restarts, and GET /sources lists id beside name.

## Done when
- the digest of the same value parsed and re-serialized twice is equal, and differs for any meaningful change (key order alone changes nothing);
- a source sent twice and after a restart keeps one id; GET /sources shows it;
- two different repositories get different ids.

Change registry-integrity, capability server: requirement identities (rename part). A rename is recorded as a claim binding the new name to the existing id; the histories and view answers stay under the id; the old name no longer creates a second source.

## Done when
- after a claimed rename, the same id answers views under the new name, byte-identical to before;
- sending under the old name afterwards does not create a second source or id;
- a claim for an unknown id is refused naming it.

Change registry-integrity, capability server: requirement immutability. A send for a source and commit the history holds answers already stored when the digest of the incoming model equals the stored artifact's digest (nothing changes), and is refused naming both digests, the source and the commit otherwise (nothing changes).

## Done when
- identical bytes resent: already stored, all stored answers byte-identical;
- different bytes for the same source+commit: refused with both digests named, stored state unchanged;
- different bytes for a new commit: stored, no refusal.

Change registry-integrity, capability server: requirement protocol. Every request carries a protocol version (the current shape is 1); every answer names the version the server speaks; a request outside the supported range is refused naming the range before anything else is read.

## Done when
- a version-1 request is served and its answers name the version;
- a version-0 request is refused naming the supported range, nothing stored, the refusal logged as one line;
- the version field is missing: refused as a missing input naming the field.

